55,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option A could cause social friction, B might be chaotic, and C is fair but temporary.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Option B with shared racks sounds like it would stop the ""ownership"" fights, but George mentioned the maintenance of frames.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,May,,"Option A brings in money for the building, which we clearly need since the ledger is so thin.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,George,,Option A is a nightmare for the treasurer. Option B's racks sound like a physical hassle. I prefer the simplicity of Option C.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option C is fair because it rotates the spots, but Option A is interesting since some people are willing to pay.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, the neighboring block's experience shows that Paid Allocation can make people avoid meetings. I can't support Option A.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@George, if the racks are too hard to use, then Option B is out. I'm leaning toward the lottery.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, but we can't ignore the budget. Still, if it ruins the atmosphere, maybe it's not worth it.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,George,,A lottery is a one-time event a year. Very little paperwork.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@George, but does a lottery solve the problem of the daily riders who really need the space?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Misaki,,A lottery is the most neutral. It prevents long-term hoarding of the dry spots.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I agree. It's the gentlest way to ensure everyone gets a turn.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,May,,"If we don't do A, then C is better than B, because B sounds like a struggle with the equipment.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,George,,I'm voting for C. It's the only one that doesn't create a permanent job for someone.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'll go with C too. It's the fairest way to handle the resentment about the spots.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I vote for C.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I vote for C.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,May,,I'll vote for C as well.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,George,,C.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Mio,,C!,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
